// A fresh public constant that only a rule's `_restrict` formula mentions.
//
// `freshNamesReport'` (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:444-452) collects the
// names of a rule with `universeBi`, which reaches the `_preRestriction`
// formula (Theory/Model/Rule.hs:424) the `_restrict` construct leaves there
// (Theory/Text/Parser.hs:175-192).  `~'foo'` is a literal, not a free
// variable, so `rewrite` returns it unchanged
// (Theory/Model/Restriction.hs:96-112) and the action fact
// `fromRuleRestriction` adds to the rule (Theory/Model/Restriction.hs:141-162)
// carries nothing.  The port collects names from the rule's premises, actions
// and conclusions, so it never sees `~'foo'`.
//
// Both engines reach `~'foo'` through the generated `Restr_R_1` restriction
// and report it under `Formula terms`, so the divergence is exactly the
// missing `Fresh public constants` topic.
//
// Mode `diverge`: the oracle reports both topics; the port reports only
// `Formula terms`.
//
// Compared slice: the wf report block.


theory S8RestrictFreshName
begin

rule R:
  [ Fr(~x) ]
  --[ _restrict( not( ~'foo' = 'a' ) ) ]->
  [ Out(~x) ]

end
